{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And if from the field of his possession.</b> That he inherits with Israel." "<b>A homer of barley.</b> And it is written that the ten baths are a homer, and there the ephah and the bath are written. Now a seed of an ephah of barley is in five shekels, and this is the decree of the King, like the price of a slave."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {1 "Reading 'the ten baths are a homer' as a reference to Ezekiel 45:11, 14; the Hebrew עשרת הבתים could also be read as 'ten baths'; resolved by the cross-reference context."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:12:57.962616998Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}